只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DSH 插件，让当前代理直接从提示词驱动其它真实 DSH 会话——创建/发送/等待回复/读取/恢复/跨工作区查找会话，并支持监控调度主任务与归档会话。A DSH plugin that lets the agent drive other real DSH sessions straight from a prompt — create, send, wait, read, resume, and find sessions across workspaces, plus monitor/schedule a main task and archive ","id":"gh:1353687670","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-session-bridge","slug":"heartmove/dsh-session-bridge","topics":["deepseek","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugins","session","session-manager"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DSH 插件，让当前代理直接从提示词驱动其它真实 DSH 会话——创建/发送/等待回复/读取/恢复/跨工作区查找会话，并支持监控调度主任务与归档会话。A DSH plugin that lets th"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"e agent drive other real DSH sessions straight from a prompt — create, send, wait, read, resume, and"},{"id":"p1s3","text":" find sessions across workspaces, plus monitor/schedule a main task and archive "},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-session-bridge — 会话桥 (Session bridge)"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Targets DSH **0.1.7-0 and later**: both the peer ranges and `package.json`'s\n`engines.dsh` declare a"},{"id":"p3s2","text":" floor only (`>=0.1.7-0`), never a ceiling. Since DSH\n**0.2.1-rc.1** `engines.dsh` decides alone (wh"},{"id":"p3s3","text":"en present, `peerDependencies` are\nignored), so the two state the same floor; verified against **0.2"},{"id":"p3s4","text":".2-alpha.3**. See\ncompatibility changes and AGENTS.md (the version\npolicy is a hard rule, guarded by"},{"id":"p3s5","text":"See\ncompatibility changes and AGENTS.md (the version\npolicy is a hard rule, guarded by `pnpm test`)."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"A DSH plugin that lets the current agent drive\nother real DSH sessions directly from a prompt — crea"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"te sessions, send\nmessages to any session, wait for and read replies, resume offline sessions,\nand f"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"ind sessions across workspaces. On top of that it can **monitor and\nschedule** a main task (watch it"},{"id":"p4s4","text":"s progress, nudge or correct its direction,\nand stop it), and **archive** sessions the same way the "},{"id":"p4s5","text":"DSH sidebar's Archive\naction does."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"> 中文文档见 README.zh.md."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## What it does"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- **Create real DSH sessions.** `session_bridge_create` makes a new main\nsession (top-level UI sessi"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"on) in the current workspace, or in another\nworkspace when you pass `workspaceId` / `cwd`. It can se"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"nd one first prompt\nand optionally block until the first reply. Provider / model / reasoning\neffort "},{"id":"p7s4","text":"are inherited from the calling session by default. An async create\n(no `waitForReply`) returns a `si"},{"id":"p7s5","text":"nceSeq` anchor for a later precise `wait`.\n- **Send messages to any session.** `session_bridge_send`"},{"id":"p7s6","text":" appends a turn\n(`mode=queue`) or injects steering into the running step (`mode=steer`), and\ncan opt"},{"id":"p7s7","text":"ionally wait for the next reply. An async send also returns a\n`sinceSeq` anchor.\n- **Wait for a repl"},{"id":"p7s8","text":"y or a segment.** `session_bridge_wait` blocks until new\nassistant output appears after `sinceSeq` ("},{"id":"p7s9","text":"default: the latest event seq at\ncall time): `waitFor=reply` (default) returns as soon as a new **te"},{"id":"p7s10","text":"xt** reply\nis readable; `waitFor=segment` returns as soon as any new **completed output\nstep** appea"},{"id":"p7s11","text":"rs (an `assistant/message` — text, reasoning, or tool-call turn),\n*without* waiting for the whole tu"},{"id":"p7s12","text":"rn, so you can observe output paragraph by\nparagraph as it is produced. With `requireTurnEnd` it add"},{"id":"p7s13","text":"itionally waits for\nthe turn to settle. Timeout / abort return the partial result rather than\nthrowi"},{"id":"p7s14","text":"ng. **An already-landed reply is never lost**: when no new output\narrives within the budget, the lat"},{"id":"p7s15","text":"est PRE-EXISTING reply/segment is returned\nwith `stale: true` (no more `(no text)`). To retrieve exa"},{"id":"p7s16","text":"ctly \"the reply to\nwhat I sent\", pass the `sinceSeq` returned by `session_bridge_send` /\n`session_br"},{"id":"p7s17","text":"idge_create` (works regardless of caller latency); `sinceSeq: -1`\ncounts existing events too, i.e. t"},{"id":"p7s18","text":"he anchor for a brand-new session.\n- **Read any session.** `session_bridge_read` folds a session's e"},{"id":"p7s19","text":"vent log into\nreadable rows — live or offline (from persistence) — with `sinceSeq` paging,\nrole filt"},{"id":"p7s20","text":"ering, and a `limit` (default 20, max 100).\n- **Read output paragraph by paragraph.** `session_bridg"},{"id":"p7s21","text":"e_segments` returns the\nsession's **completed output segments** — every finished assistant step (one"},{"id":"p7s22","text":"s` returns the\nsession's **completed output segments** — every finished assistant step (one\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"## Monitoring worker"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"`session_bridge_monitor_start` installs a timer-driven loop. Every poll it\n**observes → judges → sch"},{"id":"p9s2","text":"edules → logs** the target session:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| Observation | Action |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| A `doneKeywords` string appears in the reply and the session is idle | Wrap up and stop the watchd"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"og (log `DONE`) |\n| Idle with no pending work | Wrap up (settled) — no pointless nudging / cancellin"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"g |\n| `running` and no event for more than `stalledMs` | Record a stall → `steer` a nudge (with `use"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"Llm`, judge `offtrack`/`stuck` first) |\n| Stall repeats ≥ `maxStuckCycles` | `cancel` the session |\n"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"| Making progress | Reset the stall counter (steady) |\n| `running` and the chain-of-thought loops (o"},{"id":"p11s6","text":"n by default) | Create a successor session carrying the task → interrupt the old one (transfer, log "},{"id":"p11s7","text":"`LOOP-TRANSFER`) |\n| Loop, but the transfer budget is exhausted / `loopTransfer: false` | Interrupt "},{"id":"p11s8","text":"only (log `LOOP-CANCEL`) |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"#### What happens to subagents"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"| Scenario | Handling | Why |"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"| A. Main session loops, subagents **still running normally** | **Not cancelled**, listed in the han"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"doff (`report`, the default) | Their work is not wasted; the successor is told not to redo it and ca"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"n wait for results |\n| B. Main session loops with `loopDescendants: 'stop'` | Cancelled one by one *"},{"id":"p14s4","text":"*before** the transfer, recorded under `stopped` | You asked for a clean handoff with no orphaned wo"},{"id":"p14s5","text":"rk |\n| C. Main session loops with `loopDescendants: 'ignore'` | Neither cancelled nor mentioned | Th"},{"id":"p14s6","text":"e subagents are irrelevant to the remaining task |\n| D. **A subagent** loops (main session fine) | C"},{"id":"p14s7","text":"ancel that subagent + `steer` the main session to re-delegate; **no transfer** | The broken thing is"},{"id":"p14s8","text":" the subtask, not the task; the main session knows how to re-delegate |\n| E. A **subagent session it"},{"id":"p14s9","text":"self** is the monitored target and loops | **Cancel only, never transfer** | Its identity is a subag"},{"id":"p14s10","text":"ent; spawning a new top-level session would break the execution tree. The parent session is notified"},{"id":"p14s11","text":"t; spawning a new top-level session would break the execution tree. The parent session is notified |"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"\"Who is a subagent\" is decided with host capabilities first (`agents.isOwnedBy` / `roots()`), then\nf"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"alls back to the session header's `origin === 'subagent'` / `parentSession`, and finally treats the\n"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"session as top-level — **it can under-transfer, never mis-transfer**. The transfer chain is bounded\n"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"by `loopMaxTransfers`: a successor that loops again gets at most another transfer, then only\ninterru"},{"id":"p15s5","text":"ptions, so there is no A→B→C relay."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"- Node.js ≥ 20\n- pnpm\n- DSH `0.1.7-0` or later (`peerDependencies` and `engines.dsh` both `>=0.1.7-0"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"`;\nbuilt and tested against `0.2.2-alpha.3`)."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
